  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why snapshot",
      "items": [
        "The children of this level go into the same queue, right behind the nodes still waiting",
        "The size taken at the top of the loop is the boundary: take exactly size nodes and the level is done",
        "Without it, the for loop also takes the children it just pushed, and every node lands in one level"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Cost",
      "items": [
        "Each node enters and leaves the queue exactly once: O(n)",
        "The queue peaks at the widest level: 524,288 nodes in a perfect tree of 2^20 - 1",
        "Taking a node out must be O(1): JS array shift() and Python list.pop(0) move the whole array"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two problems, same template",
      "items": [
        "Right Side View: keep only node i = size - 1 of each level, giving [1, 3, 6, 7]",
        "Count Good Nodes: no levels needed, only the path max carried down with each node"
      ]
    }
  ]
}